<%# Deliberately does not name a licence: the repository has no LICENSE file
    yet, and a page that states one would be the site's first lie. When one
    lands, this page gains a paragraph — see ABOUT_PLAN §6a on facts that
    can't be computed. %>

<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Every line of this is public, and that is not a marketing posture — it
    is the only way the promises on these pages can be checked. A claim
    that nothing leaves your network is worth exactly as much as your
    ability to go and look.
  </p>
  <p>
    So: go and look. The code, the design documents, the decision log and
    the build log are all in the repository, including the arguments we
    lost and the things we tried and cut.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What being open buys you here</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It cannot be taken away") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Not by us losing interest, not by an acquisition, not by a change of
        terms. Copies exist; yours runs on your hardware; and the ability to
        keep running it does not depend on anyone's continued goodwill.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It can be checked") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Every privacy claim on this site corresponds to code you can read.
        If we said something that isn't true, it is true in the repository or
        it isn't true anywhere.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It can be changed") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Your household is not our target user in the abstract — it's yours,
        specifically. Fork it, cut what you don't want, add the thing your
        family actually needs. Nothing here is designed to make that hard.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "It shows its reasoning") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The repository keeps a decision log — one entry per real decision,
        including the ones that were reversed. If you want to know why the
        app works some particular way, the answer is written down rather
        than lost in someone's memory.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Helping</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    The most useful thing is to run it and say what broke. Not a bug report
    in the formal sense — just the place you got stuck, the thing you
    expected that didn't happen, the word that didn't mean what you thought.
    Software built for people who have never had an assistant is very easy
    to build for people who already understand it, and outside eyes are the
    only real defence.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    After that: writing, translation, and design help are all more valuable
    here than more features. So is telling somebody else about it — the
    argument on this site only works if enough people end up running the
    thing.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What we won't do</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Add telemetry. Add a hosted tier that gets features the self-hosted one
    doesn't. Make the good version the one where your data passes through
    somebody else. If any of that ever happens, the correct response is to
    keep running the last version that didn't — which you will be able to
    do, because that's how this is licensed and distributed.
  </p>
</section>
